Z||000000||80's BOY||08-07-2000||09:56 AM||||went for a cruise by the coast this weekend. the tach was buried PAST the red at 60mph or above. now i know my rpm range went up with the stroker kit, but it seemed sluggish too. made me nervous. fluids were okay. i just changed the filter and fluid in march. what else could it be? rpm's were alot higher than normal, even for me. is the tranny going out?||||reg||5
Z||000001||007DOUG||08-07-2000||12:15 PM||||Throttle Valve (TV) cable needs replaced. It lets the tranny know just much hard/light you're into the throttle.<P>When mine refused to kick up/down, that was the problem.<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE<BR>2 86 GT<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>BUT......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||80's BOY||08-07-2000||03:21 PM||||could it need adjustment? if so, how? i think it's shifting through all the gears okay. just ran well over redline this time.||||reg||5
Z||000003||theogre||08-07-2000||03:22 PM||||Check the TV cable first. That's fairly cheap. It could be a problem in the tranny. There's a GM TSB about the TV valve hanging up under certain conjditions. (There's a whole raft of TSB's for the TH125.) IF that's the problem it can be fixed with the tranny in the car. It requires a modification to the valve body. Not something for most to do at home.||||reg||1
